cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file. The accompanying manuscript is available as a bioRxiv preprint, given below as the preferred citation."
type: software
title: "PRECISION_paper: reproducibility package for transcription factor activities as a shared representation for drug repurposing hypotheses in breast cancer"
license: GPL-3.0
abstract: "Code and canonical result tables that reproduce every number, table and figure of the PRECISION manuscript. The manuscript uses transcription factor activities as a shared representation that links drug response in cancer cell lines to survival in breast cancer cohorts. It presents an interpretable framework for generating drug repurposing hypotheses, not a claim of predictive superiority. Triple-negative breast cancer motivates the work, the main clinical cohorts are unselected breast cancer cohorts, and the hypotheses are then checked in triple-negative cell lines and in a triple-negative cohort. The GPL-3.0 license declared here covers the code. The five data files under data/ and the derived tables under results/ are not GPL-3.0: each keeps the license of its source, recorded with its required attribution in DATA_LICENSES.md. In particular, the DepMap 25Q3 cell-line annotations are governed by the depmap.org Terms and Conditions and do not permit commercial use."
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22657695"
